1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,148
Midnight at the Gibraltar frontier.

2
00:00:03,413 --> 00:00:06,269
To walk in from Spain, you cross an airport runway.

3
00:00:06,669 --> 00:00:11,011
Since July 2026, this gate has had no routine checks.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,833
The Rock sits at the western gate of the Mediterranean.

5
00:00:15,233 --> 00:00:22,106
Historians on both sides count fourteen sieges of it, between 1309 and 1783.

6
00:00:22,506 --> 00:00:26,685
This is why everyone fought over it, told from both sides' records.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,877
In 1782, ten floating batteries came to break it.

8
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,273
In 1941, a runway was laid across the only road to Spain.

9
00:00:38,667 --> 00:00:42,429
So why, today, is the fight over it about paperwork and payrolls?

10
00:00:43,833 --> 00:00:49,290
Half a century later came a different question: can you starve a rock?

11
00:00:50,218 --> 00:00:55,907
On the twenty-first of June 1779, Madrid cut Gibraltar off from Spain.

12
00:00:56,307 --> 00:00:59,209
Spain had joined France in its war with Britain.

13
00:00:59,883 --> 00:01:05,932
By October, British intelligence put the Spanish army facing the Rock at up to fourteen thousand.

14
00:01:06,333 --> 00:01:10,606
At sea, from mid-July, a Spanish squadron sealed the port.

15
00:01:11,279 --> 00:01:17,433
Based at Algeciras, its boats were there to cut off the food reaching the Rock from Africa.

16
00:01:18,333 --> 00:01:26,124
By January 1780, thistles, dandelions and wild leeks were daily food for many; an egg cost sixpence.

17
00:01:26,524 --> 00:01:29,159
The governor, General Eliott, could hold the walls.

18
00:01:29,473 --> 00:01:31,203
The food had to come by sea.

19
00:01:32,458 --> 00:01:40,051
To break the blockade, Britain sent three relief fleets: 1780, 1781, 1782.

20
00:01:40,451 --> 00:01:45,827
Scurvy spread, until a Danish ship of lemons was brought in, garrison diaries record.

21
00:01:46,227 --> 00:01:55,097
On the twelfth of April 1781, the second relief convoy dropped anchor, and Spain's batteries opened fire on the town.

22
00:01:56,026 --> 00:01:58,046
The townspeople fled south.

